From sdavis2 at mail.nih.gov  Wed Feb  2 18:35:37 2005
From: sdavis2 at mail.nih.gov (Sean Davis)
Date: Wed Feb  2 18:35:46 2005
Subject: [BioC] non-symmetric heatmap colors
In-Reply-To: <C80ECAFA2ACC1B45BE45D133ED660ADE010BF2F3@crbsmxsusr04.pharma.aventis.com>
References: <C80ECAFA2ACC1B45BE45D133ED660ADE010BF2F3@crbsmxsusr04.pharma.aventis.com>
Message-ID: <D9ACE341-7540-11D9-8BE3-000D933565E8@mail.nih.gov>

Look at using the breaks argument.  If you do breaks=seq(-3,3,0.1) and 
use 59 colors (this is important because the number of breaks and 
colors have to match--see documentation for heatmap), you get "black" 
centered on zero and red and green symmetrically set around zero (if 
using red/green colors, obviously).

Sean

